[center][size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Kilnwarden - Web Admin[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]A web admin panel for your Enshrouded dedicated server: players, map, commands, schedules, mod updates, backups and more, served over HTTPS from inside the server itself. Phone or desktop, no extra program to run. A Kiln mod.[/color][/size]

[size=3][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/301][color=#FF6A1A]Kiln[/color][/url]  [color=#71717A]◆[/color]  [url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden][color=#FF6A1A]Source on GitHub[/color][/url]  [color=#71717A]◆[/color]  [url=https://discord.gg/7pjr8SMTfU][color=#FF6A1A]Discord[/color][/url][/b][/size]

[size=2][b][color=#F9C74F]NEEDS KILN 0.2.0-dev.31.10+[/color]  [color=#71717A]◆[/color]  [color=#F9C74F]DEDICATED SERVER ONLY[/color]  [color=#71717A]◆[/color]  [color=#F9C74F]PLAYERS NEED NOTHING[/color]  [color=#71717A]◆[/color]  [color=#F9C74F]MIT[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden/main/art/nexus_main_1280x720.png[/img][/center]

[center][url=https://discord.gg/7pjr8SMTfU][img]https://frostdev.io/kiln/discord-banner.png[/img][/url]
[size=2][color=#A1A1AA]Questions, bug reports and ideas: the Kiln Discord.[/color][/size][/center]

[quote][size=3][b][color=#F9C74F]First release: tell us how it goes[/color][/b]
[color=#D4D4D8]0.1.0 passed our offline tests on Windows and Linux, browser tests and fuzzing, and had a security review and a run on a lab server with Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.10. Let's Encrypt and Steam sign-in have only been tested against stand-ins so far. Back up [b]kiln/data/kilnwarden/[/b] with your save, and tell us what you find on [url=https://discord.gg/7pjr8SMTfU][color=#F9C74F]Discord[/color][/url] (#bug-reports), in the Bugs tab here, or on [url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden/issues][color=#F9C74F]GitHub[/color][/url], with [b]kiln/logs/kiln.log[/b].[/color][/size][/quote]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]What you get[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]The Kiln Launcher's admin pages, in any browser:[/b] players, the live map, zones, items, spawning, world and weather, combat, creatures, content, game data, saves and backups, configs, permissions and crash reports.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Every command as a form:[/b] the commands of Kiln and of every mod on your server, with pickers for players and items, sliders for numbers, switches and dropdowns, checked before they run. A console with completion and history for the rest. Save the ones you use often and pin them to the overview.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Player activity:[/b] who is on and for how long, joins, leaves and deaths, playtime per player over 7 and 30 days.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Schedules:[/b] restarts with in-game countdowns, backups, announcements and saved commands, every day at set times, every few hours, or once. Skip them when nobody is on.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Mods:[/b] switch a mod off or on for the next start, load and reload, and install or update from a zip or a GitHub release. Every package is checked (SHA-256, and minisign signatures from publishers you trust), applied at the next start, and can be rolled back once.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Metrics:[/b] players, tick and frame time, memory, CPU, GC pauses, mod faults and the time since the last save, live and for the last 30 days, with alerts.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Webhooks:[/b] Discord or any HTTPS endpoint for joins, leaves, deaths, restarts, crashes, failed saves, schedules, alerts and admin actions, with your own message text.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Accounts and roles:[/b] owner, admin, moderator, viewer and your own roles, what each may do down to single commands, two-factor sign-in, an audit log of every change. Sign in with Steam or Discord once you link your account.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]A public page if you want one:[/b] online or not, player count, a map with rough player dots, your rules and how to join. Off until you turn it on, each part on its own switch.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Your look:[/b] your server's name, colour, logo and favicon.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden/main/art/screens/commands.png[/img]
[size=2][color=#A1A1AA]Every command as a form (demo data).[/color][/size][/center]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Your server needs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/301][color=#F9C74F]Kiln[/color][/url] [b]0.2.0-dev.31.10 or later[/b] with its admin part (installed by default on a server).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Stop the server and unzip the file from the Files tab into its [b]kiln/mods/[/b] folder, so that [b]kiln/mods/kilnwarden/kiln.mod.json[/b] exists.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Start the server. [b]kiln/logs/kiln.log[/b] shows the panel's address ([b]https://127.0.0.1:15737/[/b] with the default ports: the query port + 100) and a one-time [b]setup link[/b].[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]On the server's machine, open the setup link and create your owner account. The first certificate is self-signed: check that the fingerprint your browser shows is the one in kiln.log.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Turn on two-factor sign-in in [b]My account[/b], and add your helpers in [b]Users and roles[/b].[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]The panel only answers on the server's own machine until you change that in [b]Panel settings[/b], so nobody else can reach it before you have an owner account. With Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.14 or newer, the Kiln Launcher opens it for you with [b]Open web panel[/b] on your server's page, also for a remote server over SSH.[/color][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Pick your route[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Home PC or LAN:[/b] open it on the server's machine, or with the Kiln Launcher (needs Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.14 or newer). For other devices at home, set the bind address in Panel settings and add an IP allowlist for your network.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]VPS or cloud machine:[/b] the Kiln Launcher over SSH (nothing open but SSH; needs Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.14 or newer), or your own address: open the port and get a free Let's Encrypt certificate from the panel (HTTP-01 on port 80 or TLS-ALPN-01 on port 443), or use your own certificate files. A free dynamic DNS name works.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Rented game server[/b] (FTP and a web console only): the setup link is in kiln.log, or comes from the console command [b]kilnwarden setup[/b] through Kiln's console folder over FTP. With one extra port from your host, use direct HTTPS (self-signed). Otherwise, hosted access (below).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Docker or Pterodactyl:[/b] a published port (an allocation) with [b]bind[/b] set to 0.0.0.0 in settings.json, and the data folder on the persistent volume. Or hosted access (below).[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Behind CGNAT, or IPv6 only:[/b] hosted access (below). With IPv6 only, a direct IPv6 address works too, but IPv4-only visitors can't reach it.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Your own reverse proxy:[/b] point it at the panel, turn the panel's TLS off and mark the proxy as trusted.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Step-by-step guides for each route, with the log lines you may see: [url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden/blob/main/docs/hosting-routes.md][color=#F9C74F]docs/hosting-routes.md[/color][/url].[/color][/size]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Hosted access on kiln.nexus[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#F9C74F][b]kiln.nexus is frostdev's own domain for Kiln. It has no affiliation with Nexus Mods (nexusmods.com).[/b][/color][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Hosted access gives your panel an address like [b]https://myserver.kiln.nexus[/b] with no port forwarding: your server keeps one outbound connection to frostdev.io on port 443, and browsers reach it through our relay. That makes it work on rented game servers, behind CGNAT, with IPv6 only and in containers.[/color][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]frostdev never decrypts your traffic.[/b] The relay reads only the name the browser asks for and passes the encrypted bytes through. TLS ends inside your game server, with your panel's own certificate, whose key never leaves your server, so the relay has nothing to decrypt with.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Claim your name with Discord:[/b] Panel settings > Hosted access (or the console command [b]kilnwarden claim[/b]) makes a one-time claim link signed with your panel's key. Open it, sign in with a Discord account that is a member of the Kiln Discord, and claim the name. One name per Discord account.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]What the relay sees:[/b] the panel's name, your visitors' IP addresses, when they connect and how much data flows. The relay keeps counts, not addresses. nginx in front of it records a visitor's address only when a connection fails, and keeps it 14 days. Details: [url=https://frostdev.io/kiln/privacy][color=#F9C74F]frostdev.io/kiln/privacy[/color][/url].[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Coming from a Kiln Web Admin test build?[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Kiln Web Admin is now Kilnwarden. Stop the server, delete [b]kiln/mods/kiln-webadmin/[/b], unzip Kilnwarden, and start the server: Kilnwarden moves [b]kiln/data/kiln-webadmin/[/b] to [b]kiln/data/kilnwarden/[/b] at its first start, with your accounts, settings, keys and history. It stays off, and says so in kiln.log, while the old folder is still installed. [b]webadmin setup/status/claim[/b] still work on the console.[/color][/size]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]For mod authors[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]If your mod's admin features are commands, they already show up as forms: nothing to do. For more, the panel's extension API ([b]Kilnwarden.Api[/b] 1.0.0) lets your mod add its own page (made of blocks, or your own script in a sandbox), buttons, overview widgets, settings and webhook events, with an optional dependency so your mod still loads without the panel. Start with [b]dotnet new kilnwarden-module[/b]; the template, a sample and the docs are [url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden/blob/main/docs/extension-api.md][color=#F9C74F]on GitHub[/color][/url].[/color][/size]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#F9C74F][b]Do my players need it?[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]No. It runs only on the server, and nothing changes in their game.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]Does it work on Linux?[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]Yes: on a Windows server and on Linux under Wine or Proton, the same way.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]Is it safe to open to the internet?[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]It's built for it: HTTPS, no default password, two-factor sign-in, a second password check before sensitive changes, rate limits and lockouts, a strict content policy, and an IP allowlist if you want one. Anyone who can reach the port sees the sign-in page, so use a strong password, turn on two-factor, and limit the port with the allowlist or your firewall where you can.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]Can frostdev see my panel?[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]No. Without hosted access, frostdev isn't involved at all. With hosted access, the relay passes encrypted traffic it can't read. One limit to know: the relay's operator controls the DNS for kiln.nexus, so in principle it could get a certificate for your name. We commit not to, and the [url=https://frostdev.io/kiln/privacy]Kiln privacy page[/url] says so. A kiln.nexus CAA record forbids wildcard certificates, so no single certificate can cover every panel's name.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]Where is my data?[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]In [b]kiln/data/kilnwarden/[/b] on your server: accounts, settings, keys, the audit log, metrics, schedules and webhooks. Back it up with your save.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]I forgot the owner password.[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]There is no reset yet. Stop the server and delete [b]kiln/data/kilnwarden/[/b] to start over; that also removes the settings and history. Keep your two-factor recovery codes somewhere safe.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]The map is empty.[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]The map's terrain is the game's own art, so it isn't in the zip. Copy the Kiln Launcher's game art into [b]kiln/data/kilnwarden/map-assets/[/b] to see it. Players, markers and zones show without it.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]"Restart" stops the server but it doesn't come back.[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]The panel saves, warns players and stops the server; something has to start it again. kilnctl's service does that; on other hosts the panel says "restart: unknown" and offers a plain stop. Start it again from your host's panel.[/color]

[color=#F9C74F][b]Discord sign-in?[/b][/color]
[color=#D4D4D8]Yes, through frostdev.io's Discord sign-in (the same one hosted access uses), next to local accounts and Steam sign-in.[/color][/size]
[line]
